{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Key-based, non-interactive SSH for the non-root user `clusterops` must work across all six directed peer paths using stable node names.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Each node has a locked, non-root `clusterops` identity with its own ED25519 key. Final acceptance shows public-key-only policy, stable peer-name resolution, and successful BatchMode/strict-host-key SSH to both peers from every node.","evidence_ids":["cmd-de02d9209ddb48c1","cmd-9af8cd0591e5483f","cmd-26bc016bf2dc470e","cmd-fbadd71ade8c41dc","cmd-90e86ac0adcb4251","cmd-3c262b6bc9f74764"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"SSH access for `clusterops` must be limited to the two cluster peers on each destination.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Every destination has exactly two authorized keys, corresponding to its other two nodes, and each is constrained by the expected peer source IPv4 plus `restrict`. The effective policy disables passwords, keyboard-interactive authentication, forwarding, PTYs, and user RC files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fbadd71ade8c41dc","cmd-90e86ac0adcb4251","cmd-3c262b6bc9f74764"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"`/usr/local/share/doc/ssh-cluster/OPERATIONS.md` must document topology and basic verification and recovery procedures.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The required root-owned document is present on all three nodes with identical final hashes. Captured content and final checks show topology, access model, basic verification, recovery, and socket-activation guidance.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ac53034ac2754c78","cmd-e6ac8a0098724dfd","cmd-db9e8410541347ac","cmd-54917630342c41e2","cmd-060dfa5e052045af","cmd-28f1b1d6e36b45fd","cmd-fbadd71ade8c41dc","cmd-90e86ac0adcb4251","cmd-3c262b6bc9f74764"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation is evidenced, so none remained or required reversion. Account/key creation, name and SSH policy configuration, service activation, peer authorization, documentation, and restarts all had direct task or mandatory-evidence roles. The tmpfiles probes and malformed `sed -i` attempts show no resulting state change; successful documentation rewrites removed their temporary files. Final lifecycle observations show no failed services, package damage, or abandoned task-specific temporary artifacts, and TCP/22 was already exposed before execution.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6af02a7044964cde","cmd-74f624baf22c454a","cmd-0f6ef442245b49cd","cmd-fb4e3bacc9e04b87","cmd-3f0dc094fe9c4059","cmd-c827952eb7ba4c99","cmd-1c81b42c5919495c","cmd-1cd1a816be034a8b","cmd-86c6118fc6874d0d","cmd-5ceaa10dca264808","cmd-4ae89be2ff26417b","cmd-c736ad946e6d44c6","cmd-54917630342c41e2","cmd-060dfa5e052045af","cmd-28f1b1d6e36b45fd","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node2:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node3:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Restart evidence is strong for every node: healthy pre-state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/files, and restored inbound and outbound peer connectivity were captured for node1 (`cmd-ace9e612029944e1`, `cmd-06021354769243ac`, `cmd-e922708304474bd8`, `cmd-00ccc75cfeb54937`), node2 (`cmd-52fbbe81b2b64b48`, `cmd-f533d1ac0fc9486a`, `cmd-c817d6030a604311`, `cmd-a33508e795014f60`), and node3 (`cmd-b4f70fd476484900`, `cmd-eb8119b114f947c3`, `cmd-5471f90f943f41ec`, `cmd-1be6457e95944d13`). Fixed after-executor boot identities independently agree with those transitions.","limitations":["No explicit rejected login from a non-peer or unauthorized key was captured. Peer limitation is established from the exact two-entry, source-restricted authorization state and effective SSH policy rather than a negative behavioral probe (`cmd-fbadd71ade8c41dc`, `cmd-90e86ac0adcb4251`, `cmd-3c262b6bc9f74764`).","The final documentation revision was applied after all three restart transitions (`cmd-54917630342c41e2`, `cmd-060dfa5e052045af`, `cmd-28f1b1d6e36b45fd`). Thus the exact final document hash was not itself reboot-tested, although the earlier document, SSH configuration, account data, and full peer topology were recovered. This lowers restart-protocol confidence but not task functionality because reboot persistence was not part of the public contract."]}
